+# cudagecko validation copy
+
+Purpose: write cudagecko's intermediate arrays to files, to check futhark-gecko's revcomp.fut, words.fut and sort.fut output against them
+Not for timing: timing runs use the unchanged build in ~/gecko/cudagecko
+
+## Origin
+Copied from ~/gecko/cudagecko on 2026-10-13 with cp -r
+
+## Changes (cuda/gpu_cuda_workflow.cu only)
+1. After line 314 (end of reverse complement): writes the reverse complement of the reference to cudagecko_revcomp_reference.bin (ref_len bytes, one byte per base)
+2. After line 499 in the original numbering (sorted query words copied to CPU): writes all items_read_x sorted query hashes to cudagecko_sorted_query_hashes.bin (uint64, little-endian) and positions to cudagecko_sorted_query_positions.bin (uint32, little-endian)
+Both inserted blocks are marked with the comment "VALIDATION COPY ONLY"
+
+## Build
+Modules: cuda/11.8, gcc/11.2.0
+Command: make gpu_cuda_workflow (in cuda/), built 2026-10-13 22:53 on hendrixgate04fl
+Binary: bin/gpu_cuda_workflow
+
+## Output location
+The .bin files are written to the folder the program runs from
+
+## Changes added 2026-10-14 (forward strand, query vs reference)
+3. After line 921 (sorted hits): copies sorted hits from GPU to the host buffer diagonals and writes n_hits_found uint64 values to cudagecko_sorted_hits_forward.bin
+4. After line 945 in the numbering before change 3 (filter_hits_cpu): writes n_hits_kept uint32 values each to cudagecko_filtered_hits_x_forward.bin and cudagecko_filtered_hits_y_forward.bin
+5. After line 1017 in the numbering before changes 3-4 (offsets copied to CPU): writes n_hits_kept uint32 values each to cudagecko_offsets_left_forward.bin and cudagecko_offsets_right_forward.bin
+Rebuilt 2026-10-14 with make gpu_cuda_workflow (cuda/11.8, gcc/11.2.0)
+
+## Changes added 2026-10-19 (reverse strand, query vs reverse-complemented reference)
+6. After line 1475 (filter_hits_cpu, reverse strand): writes n_hits_kept uint32 values each to cudagecko_filtered_hits_x_reverse.bin and cudagecko_filtered_hits_y_reverse.bin
+7. After line 1544 in the numbering before change 6 (offsets copied to CPU, reverse strand): writes n_hits_kept uint32 values each to cudagecko_offsets_left_reverse.bin and cudagecko_offsets_right_reverse.bin
+Rebuilt 2026-10-19 with make gpu_cuda_workflow (cuda/11.8, gcc/11.2.0)
+
+## Change added 2026-10-19 (kernels.cu, kernel_hits_load_balancing): job-range overlap fixed
+8. Original bug: blocks after G/2 (and queued jobs) computed half-size job starts that overlap the full-size jobs, so a range of sorted query words was processed twice and every hit from those words was written twice (G = 64 x number of SMs, set in gpu_cuda_workflow.cu line 75)
+   Fix: jobs 0 to G/2 keep size B; every later job starts at (G/2 + 1) * B + (job - G/2 - 1) * B/2 with size B/2, so each query word is processed once
+   Both job-range calculations replaced (first job and queued jobs), marked VALIDATION COPY ONLY
+Rebuilt 2026-10-19 13:34 with make gpu_cuda_workflow (cuda/11.8, gcc/11.2.0)
+
+## Change added 2026-10-19 (kernels.cu, kernel_hits_load_balancing): missed-hits fix (bug 3)
+9. Original: in the break branch, word_y_id = current_word_y_id moved the reference start pointer to the current 32-word chunk for the next query word, skipping that word's matches before the chunk boundary
+   Fix: assignment removed (replaced by a VALIDATION COPY ONLY comment); the next query word starts at the earlier pointer and scans forward to its matches
+Rebuilt 2026-10-19 with make gpu_cuda_workflow (cuda/11.8, gcc/11.2.0)
+
+## Change added 2026-10-19 (gpu_cuda_workflow.cu): output files appended per batch, for batched validation
+10. Before: every .bin file opened with "wb", so each batch overwrote the previous one and only the last batch was kept
+   Fix: the 11 .bin files written once per batch (lines 508 to 1559) opened with "ab"; cudagecko_revcomp_reference.bin (line 317, written once) unchanged
+   Each run must use a new, empty output folder, otherwise output is appended to old files
+Rebuilt 2026-10-19 with make gpu_cuda_workflow (cuda/11.8, gcc/11.2.0)
